1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,000
This is Task 7, Jenkins installation and continuous integration.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Jenkins is an automation server.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:19,000
It watches the repository, and for every change it runs the build and the tests automatically, so that mistakes are found in minutes, not weeks.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
This is continuous integration.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Here Jenkins runs as a Docker container.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:44,000
These lines of its compose file show the setup: the port 8090, only reachable from this computer, a named volume that keeps jobs and builds, the Docker socket so Jenkins can build images, our repository mounted read only, and a local image registry on port 5000.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The Jenkins image is built from our own Dockerfile.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:01:08,000
It starts from the official long term support Jenkins, and adds what our pipeline needs: Python three point eleven, the same version as production, Chromium and chromedriver for the Selenium tests, and the Docker command line tool.

9
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The plugins list is short: pipeline, Git, JUnit for test reports, credentials binding, the stage view, and timestamps.

10
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:30,000
To start Jenkins, the documented procedure is docker compose up dash d, in the deploy slash jenkins folder, then wait about a minute.

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Now I check that it is really running: both containers are up, and the login page answers with the Jenkins version in its response header.

12
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
If Jenkins were stopped, this is the command I would run.

13
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Now an important distinction.

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Three different things can be true.

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
First: a Jenkinsfile exists in the repository.

16
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
That is only a file.

17
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Git ls files proves it is tracked, and the log shows who changed it and why.

18
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
But a file alone runs nothing.

19
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Second: a job is configured in Jenkins.

20
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:22,000
I ask Jenkins for the job configuration, using the admin password that the command reads from the environment file, without displaying it.

21
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The configuration says: poll the Git repository every five minutes, take the branch from the BRANCH parameter, read the pipeline from the file called Jenkinsfile, and the repository is the mounted project.

22
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
The job has three parameters.

23
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Third, and the only one that proves anything: the job actually ran.

24
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
This is the real build history from Jenkins.

25
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Eleven builds.

26
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Most are success.

27
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Builds two and nine are failures: those are the deliberate defect experiments of Task 10.

28
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Build eleven, the most recent, succeeded.

29
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:09,000
The names show the version and the commit that each build used.

30
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Here are the stages of build eleven, with the status and the time of each.

31
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Checkout, install dependencies, static checks, which is the linting, unit and integration tests, the Selenium tests, packaging the source, building the images, publishing, deploying and the health check.

32
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
All success.

33
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,000
The whole pipeline took about one hundred and three seconds.

34
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Note: this build is from the twentieth of October.

35
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:50,000
It is real, but it is a historic build, not one I started just now.

36
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Finally, evidence from the console log of build eleven.

37
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Pip install runs for the dependencies.

38
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Flake8 is the linter.

39
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Eighty five unit and integration tests passed.

40
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Five Selenium tests passed, and the other eighty five were deselected, as intended.

41
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Then the checksum of the source archive is created, and the build finishes with SUCCESS.

42
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
If a stage had failed, this is where the failure would be.


